.\" jailopsd.8, installed as /usr/local/share/man/man8/jailopsd.8
.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt JAILOPSD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jailopsd
.Nd the JailOps daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar file
.Op Fl dev
.Op Fl web | Fl no-web
.Op Fl appliance-modules Ar list
.Nm
.Fl check-config
.Op Fl config Ar file
.Op Fl web | Fl no-web
.Op Fl appliance-modules Ar list
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the per-host daemon of JailOps, a ZFS-native platform for
.Fx
jails.
It serves the REST API and, when enabled, the web console; it keeps the
desired state of jails, images, networks and firewall policies in a SQLite
database and reconciles the host against it.
It runs unprivileged, as the user
.Sy jailops ,
and reaches the system (ZFS, jail(8), pf(4), interfaces) only through the
privileged helper
.Xr jailops-priv 8
over its unix socket.
.Pp
The configuration file is YAML; unknown keys are an error.
The sample installed next to it lists every key.
By default the API is served on the unix socket
.Pa /var/run/jailops/jailops.sock ;
a TLS listener (TLS 1.3 only) is opened when
.Sy listen.https.address
is set, and the console when
.Sy web.enabled
is true.
Only root (uid 0) is recognised on the unix socket, as the host's recovery
access; every other client signs in with a JailOps user, an API token or a
client certificate.
.Pp
Two routes answer without credentials, for monitors and load balancers:
.Pa /healthz
is liveness (the process answers HTTP) and always says
.Dq ok ;
.Pa /readyz
answers 200
.Dq ok
only when start-up has finished, the helper answers a read-only call and the
database answers a query, and 503
.Dq not ready: Ar class
otherwise, where
.Ar class
is starting, stopping, helper, storage or store.
The answer is cached for two seconds.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl config Ar file
The configuration file.
The default is
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/jailopsd.yaml .
.It Fl check-config
Validate the configuration and exit.
.It Fl web
Serve the web console whatever
.Sy web.enabled
says, and open the TLS listener on port 39110 when none is configured.
.It Fl no-web
Serve no web console whatever
.Sy web.enabled
says.
The API is unchanged.
.Fl web
and
.Fl no-web
exclude each other.
.It Fl appliance-modules Ar list
The host management modules
.Va jailops_appliance
of
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
turns on, comma separated, or
.Sy all :
added to
.Sy host.manage.modules .
What the helper changes is decided by its own list
.Pq Xr jailops-priv 8 ;
a module only the daemon lists answers
.Sy not_managed .
.It Fl dev
Development: run the privileged operations in the daemon's own process.
Needs root; never used by the rc.d script.
.It Cm version
Print the version and exit.
.Fl -version
does the same.
.El
.Sh RC.CONF
The rc.d script
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/jailopsd
runs the daemon under
.Xr daemon 8
as the user
.Sy jailops
and sends its output to syslog with the tag
.Sy jailopsd .
It requires
.Sy jailops_priv ,
.Sy NETWORKING ,
.Sy pf
and
.Sy syslogd .
.Bl -tag -width jailopsd_config
.It Va jailopsd_enable
Set to
.Dq YES
to start the daemon at boot.
.It Va jailopsd_config
The configuration file.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/jailopsd.yaml .
.It Va jailopsd_runas
The unprivileged user.
Default
.Sy jailops .
.It Va jailopsd_web
.Dq YES
passes
.Fl web ,
.Dq NO
passes
.Fl no-web ;
unset, the configuration decides.
.It Va jailops_appliance
.Dq YES
passes
.Fl appliance-modules
with
.Va jailops_appliance_modules
(default: all modules), and, after every start while no administrator exists,
prints a new setup token and the console's addresses on
.Pa /dev/console
and to syslog
.Pq Dq service jailopsd setuptoken .
.El
.Pp
At boot
.Sy jailops_priv
starts first and at shutdown it stops last.
The two are one service, the helper being the part that runs as root.
A start of
.Nm
by hand while the helper is not running starts the helper first, as
.Xr rc.subr 8
does for a dependency (it prints that the helper will be forced to start),
and a stop of
.Nm
stops the helper after it, so
.Cm restart
replaces both.
A start while the helper still runs a binary that has been replaced since
it started (a package upgrade) warns that the helper needs a restart too.
.Cm status
also says whether the helper runs: without it the daemon serves, but changes
nothing on the host, and it reconnects once the helper is back.
After an upgrade of the package, restart the pair:
.Dl service jailopsd restart
.Pp
The configuration is validated as the daemon's user with
.Dl service jailopsd checkconfig
and a start refuses a configuration that does not validate.
The one-time token of the first-run setup (appliance mode), a new one on every
call, is printed as root by
.Dl service jailopsd setuptoken
There is no
.Cm reload :
the configuration is read at start.
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGTERM , Dv SIGINT
Stop: the listeners close and running operations are cancelled.
.It Dv SIGHUP
Ignored by design.
A renewed TLS certificate and key are picked up without a restart (the files
are checked at most every fifteen seconds).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/jailopsd.yaml
The configuration; the installed sample is
.Pa jailopsd.yaml.sample .
.It Pa /var/run/jailops/jailops.sock
The API socket.
.It Pa /var/run/jailopsd.pid
The pid of the daemon under rc.d.
.It Pa /var/run/jailopsd-daemon.pid
The pid of its
.Xr daemon 8
supervisor.
.It Pa /var/db/jailops
The data directory: database, seal key, TLS material, operation journal
.Pq Sy data_dir .
.It Pa /var/db/jailops/state
The state dataset, mounted outside the storage root
.Pq Sy state_dir .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jailops/jails
The rendered jail.conf files
.Pq Sy conf_dir ,
shared with the helper.
.It Pa /var/run/jailops-priv/priv.sock
The socket of
.Xr jailops-priv 8
.Pq Sy priv.socket ;
the former
.Pa /var/run/jailops/priv.sock
means this path.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success, or a valid configuration with
.Fl check-config .
.It 1
The configuration does not load, or the daemon could not start or failed
while running.
.It 2
Usage: an unknown flag, an unexpected argument, or
.Fl web
together with
.Fl no-web .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jailops 1 ,
.Xr jailops-sync 1 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Xr jailops-backupd 8 ,
.Xr jailops-priv 8
.Pp
The design and the guides are installed under
.Pa /usr/local/share/doc/jailops .
.Sh SETUP
A first-time host is set up with
.Dl jailops-priv init -pool POOL
which creates the user, the datasets and both configuration files; with
.Va jailops_appliance
the first start of
.Sy jailops_priv
does it.
The first administrator is created with the setup token in the web console
.Pq Li POST /api/v1/setup
or as root with
.Dl jailops user create NAME --admin --password-prompt
